{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.925377Z","id":"6011cecd1752156802dacadc92021f4cdb331a0735a154c7d2498418156e9151","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design §9.3 says config.ts refuses a full reel outside 60–80 s and a short cut outside 40–50 s. While web/reel/reel.toml lists only some vignettes (one, realtime, today: 12.2 s in full), parseReel cannot apply that check, so it lives in checkCuts, which config.test.ts exercises but no recorder or composer calls. The composition (`//web/reel:reel`, phase 2) should call it once reel.toml lists every vignette of spec §3.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"cfb0132daace495a1f72d9ef133ac081a4b32163497cf9da3e9d4d621e26f664"},"suggested_fix":"Call checkCuts from the composition's entry point (and the composer's own reel.toml check) when reel.toml names all nine vignettes.","summary":"Nothing calls checkCuts yet: parseReel does not hold reel.toml to the 60–80 s full and 40–50 s short cuts","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/reel.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.925763Z","id":"b1cb9ebc6897ab71a4bc79acdc82c77bd4a01a12f174a92a500dddc506edb6b6","body":{"detail":"The recorder imports only web/e2e/fixtures.ts, time.ts and hosted-helpers.ts and reads web/package.json, but //web:files is the whole web project (shell, bridge, unit tests, every e2e spec). Spec §8 lists the e2e helpers it imports as the input. A recording takes tens of seconds per vignette, and only `just reel` pays it, but a test edit invalidating every <id>_fast and later <id>_frames is wasted work. A narrower input needs web/BUILD.bazel to split the e2e helpers out of :files_tests (two copy_to_bin of one file conflict).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"c3c695679dc521554c2b9c5bfeaeb100d62971cc664d1bdbf9fe4164b434b7f0"},"suggested_fix":"In web/BUILD.bazel, a copy_to_bin of web/e2e/*.ts minus *.spec.ts (taken out of :files_tests' glob) plus package.json, and the reel's srcs name that instead of //web:files.","summary":"Every recording reads all of //web:files, so an edit to any web unit or browser test re-records every vignette","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.926Z","id":"a5b80597b38f3d77c84a282bbe5b7c03be9607b762543a58ae3ee59db7848e51","body":{"detail":"hostedDaemon in web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts calls test.skip when the daemon takes another port, which only works inside a Playwright test, so the recorder restates its [hosted] config (public_origin, setup_secret_env) and fails instead. Factoring a startHosted() that both call would keep one copy of that config, at the cost of touching the e2e helpers (and so rerunning every browser test) in the reel's first change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"e84d9b83eb5558019b168d93b6a16079470631fecf0c695eeadd665dedb50911"},"summary":"Factor a test-free hosted daemon start out of web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts instead of restating its config here","tags":["revisit:the [hosted] config hostedDaemon writes changes, or a second recorder needs it","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.926251Z","id":"e373ab8bb26916a77a551a363ff8bf15eb0fb7a493db0131c7fb0acb29b1f7e5","body":{"detail":"Playwright's recordVideo scales a page's screencast down to fit the size it is given, never up: at size 1600 × 1000 a 1280 × 800 viewport at device scale 1.25 recorded as 1280 × 800 in the top left corner of a grey 1600 × 1000 frame. So fast mode records at the viewport's size; the capture's 1600 × 1000 device pixels (spec §5) come from deterministic mode (CDP screenshots). A reel composed from fast clips (`reel_fast`, spec §8) must scale them up or frame them smaller.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"f23a5ef1a46edaf27ef06dbcec997c8ae87cd341ce7c388121c513fbf4b4a81f"},"summary":"The fast clip is 1280 × 800 (the viewport's CSS size), not the capture's 1600 × 1000","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/reel.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:24.610858Z","id":"afc20ef71dc4ccd94cfb2d3a902250b55f496f77768c166ce10301d2bdd2e3c2","body":{"detail":"The recorder imports only web/e2e/fixtures.ts, time.ts and hosted-helpers.ts and reads web/package.json, but //web:files is the whole web project (shell, bridge, unit tests, every e2e spec). Spec §8 lists the e2e helpers it imports as the input. A recording takes tens of seconds per vignette, and only `just reel` pays it, but a test edit invalidating every <id>_fast and <id>_frames is wasted work. A narrower input needs web/BUILD.bazel to split the e2e helpers out of :files_tests (two copy_to_bin of one file conflict).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"c3c695679dc521554c2b9c5bfeaeb100d62971cc664d1bdbf9fe4164b434b7f0"},"suggested_fix":"In web/BUILD.bazel, a copy_to_bin of web/e2e/*.ts minus *.spec.ts (taken out of :files_tests' glob) plus package.json, and the reel's srcs name that instead of //web:files.","summary":"Every recording reads all of //web:files, so an edit to any web unit or browser test re-records every vignette","supersedes":"b1cb9ebc6897ab71a4bc79acdc82c77bd4a01a12f174a92a500dddc506edb6b6","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:25.643188Z","id":"34183bb704faa93665d8469785e43fedfdf0bfac220225c3976fce572a14680e","body":{"detail":"hostedDaemon in web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts calls test.skip when the daemon takes another port, which only works inside a Playwright test, so the recorder restates its [hosted] config (public_origin, setup_secret_env) and fails instead. Factoring a startHosted() that both call would keep one copy of that config, at the cost of touching the e2e helpers (and so rerunning every browser test) in the reel's first change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"cf00ca93ad8ce8dff77717c6360b13e077db56b9664e3b5af9a71e2ca9c12f3f"},"summary":"Factor a test-free hosted daemon start out of web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts instead of restating its config here","supersedes":"a5b80597b38f3d77c84a282bbe5b7c03be9607b762543a58ae3ee59db7848e51","tags":["revisit:the [hosted] config hostedDaemon writes changes, or a second recorder needs it","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:25.977990Z","id":"003f436301545968a3c29f12a00251583a252a98b556baea7931b694f99228e2","body":{"detail":"Playwright's recordVideo scales a page's screencast down to fit the size it is given, never up: at size 1600 × 1000 a 1280 × 800 viewport at device scale 1.25 recorded as 1280 × 800 in the top left corner of a grey 1600 × 1000 frame. So fast mode records at the viewport's size; the capture's 1600 × 1000 device pixels (spec §5) come from deterministic mode (CDP screenshots with a clip at the page's devicePixelRatio, web/reel/camera.ts). A reel composed from fast clips (`reel_fast`, spec §8) must scale them up or frame them smaller.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"a3cd579606f12e65f71cbf8dbb1978c9a7f0b22f2c4122db87f804fe3355af94"},"summary":"The fast clip is 1280 × 800 (the viewport's CSS size), not the capture's 1600 × 1000","supersedes":"e373ab8bb26916a77a551a363ff8bf15eb0fb7a493db0131c7fb0acb29b1f7e5","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.131643Z","id":"51a9983becc7e62126858721009a2e0f54718a7b8c38ef8154c0830301574090","body":{"detail":"FREEZE_IN keeps each animation's first-seen time in Animation.id, the one piece of per-animation state that every JavaScript world shares (the recorder evaluates in an isolated world or over the DevTools protocol, and getAnimations() hands each world its own wrappers). A page that names its animations, reads their ids, or reads their playState or currentTime would see the recorder's values: a vignette filming such a page would show it behaving differently than it does for a person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"34b11bbb1b3b1930ed0583d3cf054ab3d4f833563aa0139ae2dd952e1cb1fe24"},"suggested_fix":"Keep first-seen times recorder-side, keyed by the DevTools protocol's object identity (a RemoteObject per animation in one isolated world held for the frame's life), and leave id alone.","summary":"The deterministic camera writes `reel@<ms>` into the id of every animation on the page, and pauses them through the page's own Animation objects","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.131751Z","id":"3f211f601e38bfd9fab3b9d454aa7379837327c7772bd7bb15136fbefe7d431e","body":{"detail":"quiet() waits for the page's in-flight requests (Playwright request events: the page's frames, not its shared or service workers) and then drains each frame's task queue with a MessageChannel round trip, frames inside first and the page last, twice over. A message one renderer posts to another (the artifact frame's clax:peer-at to the shell, which places the name tags) is very likely, not certain, to have run before the screenshot. realtime.ts waits for each person's step to reach Alex's frame (clax:peers, db/changed) before the film moves on; what one renderer then tells another inside a frame is what the drain covers. //web/reel:realtime_determinism passed on its runs on one machine; a failure there names the first differing frame and keeps the pair in the test's outputs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"ccc105d2800f2d28c59797512858d0f53f4753a95a44221bfad6ab65528f4ee8"},"suggested_fix":"If a pair ever differs on a tag or arrow, keep the artifact frame in the shell's process for the deterministic camera (Chromium --disable-features=IsolateOrigins,site-per-process, merged with Playwright's own --disable-features list, which a second flag would replace).","summary":"A frame is taken once the page's requests are done and each frame's queued tasks have run, which orders work inside a process but only very likely across processes","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.131937Z","id":"14d31b897f7d50ade6ca87cc71c7688ba4f820137ec50c733576f80403c2efde","body":{"detail":"determinism.sh runs `node reel/record.ts` twice; the recorder needs the web project laid out as bazel/js/npm_script.mjs lays it out (Node, the project's packages, the e2e helpers it imports, the warmed clax and the browsers read where Bazel put them), which a bare sh_test's runfiles do not give. The test stays tagged manual, exclusive, no-sandbox and no-remote, as a recording is.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":99},"content_hash":"9c5f83028781f7489593f27001c3f22f5fb6c19ef1282bc1bf4727d34bd245bb"},"summary":"realtime_determinism is an npm_script_test that runs determinism.sh (pnpm run reel:determinism), not a bare sh_test","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:34:42.822110Z","id":"bf88d144c2882a15dba6728f6024079144bc5225963d67369378d9931114ffbb","body":{"detail":"Clicking from the gallery into an artifact (web/reel/vignettes/coldopen.ts, before its keeper tab) made the new page request /_clax/shell/stream-worker-<hash>.js; the page's `request` event added it to `pending`, but no `requestfinished` or `requestfailed` came for it, so quiet() failed: \"a frame waited 10 s on http://localhost:<port>/_clax/shell/stream-worker-J1zpXLYI.js\". The gallery's own load during setup did not hit this, as `pending` is only tracked once the camera rolls. coldopen.ts:131:136 works around it with a second, unfilmed tab on the gallery that keeps the shared worker alive, so the artifact page joins it without fetching its script.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":166},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"218a2fbcd9bc165c64e034f9176374809cf6808c201812145cee279aa6f550bf"},"suggested_fix":"Leave out of `pending` a request made for a worker (its script fetch), or count it done once its response is received; then drop the keeper tab in coldopen.ts.","summary":"A navigation during play fails the deterministic camera: the shell's shared stream worker script is requested and never seen to finish","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:45:23.652427Z","id":"f36fff73fc1a61d6083d0a47ed45de82efcc538fc77a157db4690720182fc06c","body":{"detail":"SEEDED_RANDOM (an init script on the camera's context in deterministic mode) replaces Math.random with mulberry32 from one seed, so the shell's backoff jitter (web/shell/src/lifecycle.ts:82, used from page code) and the gallery's random haiku (web/shell/src/view/haiku.ts:5) draw the same numbers each run, as long as the calls come in the same order. The shell's stream runs in a SharedWorker (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts:601 retries with backoff()), where no init script reaches: a stream retry there waits a random, real-time amount. crypto.getRandomValues and crypto.randomUUID are untouched; an ID drawn with them that reaches the screen differs per run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"e643f97fb275d8641d2f5e7119aa08c36c7a28138902d86f263c931afba5a203"},"suggested_fix":"If a vignette films a stream retry, or shows a client-minted ID, seed the worker through a CDP Target.setAutoAttach session (Runtime.evaluate in the worker before it runs) or keep that state off camera.","summary":"A deterministic camera seeds Math.random in its pages' documents, but not in their workers, and crypto.getRandomValues stays random","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:45:23.652659Z","id":"0ff266c9f91ee4046eb8cc4a6cabf9268b02ce575264aea717749ab5d0028479","body":{"detail":"The deterministic camera steps Playwright's clock and the page's animations, but the text caret's blink is driven by the renderer (its caret blink timer), which neither reaches. realtime films Alex's page with no focused field, so it is not affected; a vignette whose camera types into a field (a composer, a search box) would see frames differ by the caret alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":269},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"5a3fabe5514afc231375feee3ad070b22e6202596bdfa34d983d9219ae12a7c4"},"suggested_fix":"For a deterministic camera, give focused fields `caret-color: transparent` with an init stylesheet, or draw the caret as the reel's own steady bar; or set the blink interval to 0 if the pinned Chromium honours a flag for it.","summary":"A focused text field's caret blinks on Chromium's own timer, not the page's clock: a vignette that films one gets the caret on or off by real timing","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:45:23.652703Z","id":"310f269349d1583d314a322f924a437d48a61a8f33b3b4f2121456d59dc3b11c","body":{"detail":"The camera's context clock starts at REEL_EPOCH (2026-11-03T09:41:00Z) and the deterministic camera rolls at a multiple of 2 s after it; the daemon stamps comments, versions and drafts with the machine's real time. A view that shows a stamp relative to now (\"2 minutes ago\", \"in 7 days\") compares a real time with a fixed one, so it reads oddly and changes from run to run as the real date moves. realtime shows none on camera.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":154},"content_hash":"a61fe77e63d657148116065c55f4ffd58fbf75d15a59fc6af2f63e43323f21d8"},"suggested_fix":"Run the vignette's daemon on a clock fixed to REEL_EPOCH as well (a test-only clock override on the daemon), or keep stamped times off camera.","summary":"Times the daemon stamps are real, while the camera's pages read REEL_EPOCH plus their setup: a relative time between the two is neither fixed nor sensible","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:45:23.653399Z","id":"5e319e7ed27d34389f6053cef28dbe43176c4c3bcff795d69db321ee4d2f8898","body":{"detail":"With both, //web/reel:realtime_determinism passed three times idle and once with a CPU burner on every core (see the commit that recorded this).","kind":"comment","references":"3f211f601e38bfd9fab3b9d454aa7379837327c7772bd7bb15136fbefe7d431e","summary":"quiet() no longer waits on the shell's event stream when it is fetched as a stream (/api/stream, or an Accept of text/event-stream), only on requests that end; and the renderers' animation timelines are stopped (Animation.setPlaybackRate 0), so nothing started between two freezes moves on real time","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:46:49.403221Z","id":"ec233ccf007effaf05f4008bc36e0a3d9f13da96c9317ad0e5b9e0eb51c776de","body":{"detail":"hostedDaemon in web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts calls test.skip when the daemon takes another port, which only works inside a Playwright test, so the recorder restates its [hosted] config (public_origin, setup_secret_env) and fails instead. Factoring a startHosted() that both call would keep one copy of that config, at the cost of touching the e2e helpers (and so rerunning every browser test) in the reel's first change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"cf00ca93ad8ce8dff77717c6360b13e077db56b9664e3b5af9a71e2ca9c12f3f"},"summary":"Factor a test-free hosted daemon start out of web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts instead of restating its config here","supersedes":"34183bb704faa93665d8469785e43fedfdf0bfac220225c3976fce572a14680e","tags":["revisit:the [hosted] config hostedDaemon writes changes, or a second recorder needs it","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:46:49.485329Z","id":"d461bfc8551d0a4cdaac125d5912257657f4f9fd0cf0bf59eba39bcd875bc4b1","body":{"detail":"Playwright's recordVideo scales a page's screencast down to fit the size it is given, never up: at size 1600 × 1000 a 1280 × 800 viewport at device scale 1.25 recorded as 1280 × 800 in the top left corner of a grey 1600 × 1000 frame. So fast mode records at the viewport's size; the capture's 1600 × 1000 device pixels (spec §5) come from deterministic mode (CDP screenshots with a clip at the page's devicePixelRatio, web/reel/camera.ts). A reel composed from fast clips (`reel_fast`, spec §8) must scale them up or frame them smaller.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"a3cd579606f12e65f71cbf8dbb1978c9a7f0b22f2c4122db87f804fe3355af94"},"summary":"The fast clip is 1280 × 800 (the viewport's CSS size), not the capture's 1600 × 1000","supersedes":"003f436301545968a3c29f12a00251583a252a98b556baea7931b694f99228e2","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:46:49.567795Z","id":"75f782cc7dede74b4ad3a7359e109f299eb023cdfa39f1f6c9b40dbdd95a8baf","body":{"detail":"FREEZE_IN keeps each animation's first-seen time in Animation.id, the one piece of per-animation state that every JavaScript world shares (the recorder evaluates in an isolated world or over the DevTools protocol, and getAnimations() hands each world its own wrappers). A page that names its animations, reads their ids, or reads their playState or currentTime would see the recorder's values: a vignette filming such a page would show it behaving differently than it does for a person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"c0a90d004af08911ad777c0476184cd1adfbe9e17a13b9aa5ae48578a39ad316"},"suggested_fix":"Keep first-seen times recorder-side, keyed by the DevTools protocol's object identity (a RemoteObject per animation in one isolated world held for the frame's life), and leave id alone.","summary":"The deterministic camera writes `reel@<ms>` into the id of every animation on the page, and pauses them through the page's own Animation objects","supersedes":"51a9983becc7e62126858721009a2e0f54718a7b8c38ef8154c0830301574090","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:46:49.649756Z","id":"1e679dbcaa945d521fb45e7df8a297cf98f4d004366b1a728b8568b05d79ef9c","body":{"detail":"quiet() waits for the page's in-flight requests (Playwright request events: the page's frames, not its shared or service workers) and then drains each frame's task queue with a MessageChannel round trip, frames inside first and the page last, twice over. A message one renderer posts to another (the artifact frame's clax:peer-at to the shell, which places the name tags) is very likely, not certain, to have run before the screenshot. realtime.ts waits for each person's step to reach Alex's frame (clax:peers, db/changed) before the film moves on; what one renderer then tells another inside a frame is what the drain covers. //web/reel:realtime_determinism passed on its runs on one machine; a failure there names the first differing frame and keeps the pair in the test's outputs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":244},"end":{"line":261},"content_hash":"ee981fb0481d7f641e0bd529320fa973c4ddee5cd00d755f73712a1416ff959f"},"suggested_fix":"If a pair ever differs on a tag or arrow, keep the artifact frame in the shell's process for the deterministic camera (Chromium --disable-features=IsolateOrigins,site-per-process, merged with Playwright's own --disable-features list, which a second flag would replace).","summary":"A frame is taken once the page's requests are done and each frame's queued tasks have run, which orders work inside a process but only very likely across processes","supersedes":"3f211f601e38bfd9fab3b9d454aa7379837327c7772bd7bb15136fbefe7d431e","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:46:49.732501Z","id":"39cffeb64310dfd84ec578012bc89136d02a1068bba4452a8e2c108f04f326a4","body":{"detail":"determinism.sh runs `node reel/record.ts` twice; the recorder needs the web project laid out as bazel/js/npm_script.mjs lays it out (Node, the project's packages, the e2e helpers it imports, the warmed clax and the browsers read where Bazel put them), which a bare sh_test's runfiles do not give. The test stays tagged manual, exclusive, no-sandbox and no-remote, as a recording is.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"9c5f83028781f7489593f27001c3f22f5fb6c19ef1282bc1bf4727d34bd245bb"},"summary":"realtime_determinism is an npm_script_test that runs determinism.sh (pnpm run reel:determinism), not a bare sh_test","supersedes":"14d31b897f7d50ade6ca87cc71c7688ba4f820137ec50c733576f80403c2efde","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:00:02.727213Z","id":"c1a240eae37cbfd892c4a9c3ae7d48c68f73b04ac28ce179b6ac8b8eb5458d37","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0ff266c9f91ee4046eb8cc4a6cabf9268b02ce575264aea717749ab5d0028479","summary":"caret-animation: manual holds the caret still and shown on the pinned Chromium: web/reel/vignettes/coldopen.ts adds it to the camera's documents (STILL_CARET), and //web/reel:coldopen_determinism passed twice while the film types into New's dialog (254 frames identical). Without it frames 47 to 59 differed only by the caret.","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:00:02.797632Z","id":"4a75efdd14c1bb8370b2f5be1b0a94ddefd1819ae56d0f274b826f7eeab8c1b8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bf88d144c2882a15dba6728f6024079144bc5225963d67369378d9931114ffbb","summary":"A second failure on the same path: Director.click on a control that navigates rolls its 150 ms after-click hold while the old page's frames go, and freeze() then fails in reach() with \"no frame http://<id>.localhost:<port>/_clax/v/1/ in http://localhost:<port>/a/<id>\". web/reel/vignettes/coldopen.ts navClick works around it (the press ring, then the press offstage, and no frame until the next page's content frame is there). freeze() could skip a frame that is detached or no longer in the frame tree.","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.258726Z","id":"f80cdd2bd4f38fb14b796881223ace5ab712e029a0c52744f7431ded5d89f9ac","body":{"detail":"A shell document that loads anew while the camera rolls (the agent vignette's Reload, web/reel/vignettes/agent.ts) requests /_clax/shell/stream-worker-<hash>.js again (new SharedWorker in web/shell/src/stream.ts:92), and Playwright reports the request on the page (resourceType script, no sec-fetch-dest header) but never reports it finished, so quiet() waited 10 s and failed. The exemption matches that path alone; it couples the recorder to the shell's build output name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"10818436b546fd49acf98f111ef765403dd5e55ad7c260604aa4cc1925af86af"},"suggested_fix":"Recognise a shared worker's script request by what Chromium says of it (Network.requestWillBeSent type or initiator over CDP) instead of its path.","summary":"The deterministic camera exempts the shell's shared worker script by its URL path, so a renamed or moved worker would make every Reload-type navigation stall a frame for QUIET_MS","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.258790Z","id":"2dcbc3afe05dc5fbec296f60ba2b454e2c102fb3846dfa17b180ce25af06e35f","body":{"detail":"Needed for a Reload during a roll: the old content frame vanished between page.frames() and its lookup, which failed the recording (no frame <v1 url>). The skipped document is reached at the next frame. A document mid-navigation that shows on a screenshot unfrozen could differ between runs; the agent vignette avoids it by waiting for the new shell in the Reload click's `landed` (web/reel/director.ts click), so no frame is taken mid-load. //web/reel:agent_determinism passes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":230},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"7c5cbd9c5a38486daf58465347d839ade08957d094774c1af59a73cf2c974bf0"},"summary":"inEach skips a frame the page is replacing (detached, or not found in the frame tree by its URL): that document's animations are not frozen and its queue not drained for that one frame","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.258820Z","id":"e80b6b28fd36e065eb559862d2afd4cf3384791c392943526f181f1f9ce2e3d9","body":{"detail":"The daemons keep real time and have no clock a test can set (the store's clock is SystemClock, crates/clax-server/src/core.rs:145). With the camera ahead of them (2026-11-03) the agent vignette read \"7 d ago\" and a working clock of 160:30:27 that changed between two renders. Behind them, their times clamp to \"just now\" and 0:00 (web/shell/src/format.ts relativeTime, web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts clock) on any day. A ticking working clock would need a daemon clock the recorder sets.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"f6e9130cbc053b2e93f1da821d275d9aa2dd73b41308bf0f796b256d2bf8671c"},"summary":"REEL_EPOCH is in the past (2025-11-03): every time a daemon stamps reads \"just now\" and every working clock reads 0:00 and never ticks on film","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.258844Z","id":"9d6e385e43cefe45bf1dda81a51a2ccb019811fdf23eb31fb1e5a6d89c0b9ecb","body":{"detail":"The caret blinks on the browser's own timer, which page.clock does not hold: //web/reel:agent_determinism failed on frames 173-184 where one run showed the composer's caret and the other did not. Playwright's own screenshots hide the caret by default for the same reason.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"d0248b0e8ff67da306d76159bcfda68d3e541bed581d558183ddafadf37b341e"},"summary":"The deterministic camera hides every text caret (NO_CARET), so the film shows no caret while Alex types","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:40.263287Z","id":"d966bd6e8abce274276c0def826f1e2eece6c136a1aec92d6dde4fd15cef655b","body":{"detail":"Measured with web/reel/seed/starchase.html in //web/reel:game_frames: the content frame's first animation frame ran at REEL time +5 ms in one run and +8 ms in another (playwright-core's injected clock, getTimeToNextFrame() = 16 - ticks % 16, ticks counted from the document's own load). Within a 33 ms film frame two or three callbacks run, at times whose phase differs per run, so a page that reads Date.now() or performance.now() per animation frame, or steps once per callback, films different pixels each run, although this comment says animation frames run on the camera's clock. web/reel/seed/starchase.html steps its game on 30ths of a second of Date.now() (ceil((now - 0.5) / (100/3))) to be filmed the same. Pages the reel films with continuous animation need the same, or the camera needs to align each document's animation frames to its film frames.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"64a4f5543c48ddf60a5491543913bc38ea8d8c04ab5bdd7e0a6c9b72c5a80f05"},"summary":"Date.now() read in an animation frame is not the same from run to run under the deterministic camera: Playwright's fake requestAnimationFrame fires on a 16 ms grid of each document's own performance.now() origin","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:40.263802Z","id":"9043459ca48abd398e8ca293b6edf8528f0942c4460c54c71df3d488b03c3c11","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0ff266c9f91ee4046eb8cc4a6cabf9268b02ce575264aea717749ab5d0028479","span":{"start":{"line":269},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"5a3fabe5514afc231375feee3ad070b22e6202596bdfa34d983d9219ae12a7c4"},"summary":"`caret-animation: manual` on text fields keeps the caret drawn without blinking: web/reel/vignettes/game.ts:66:83 sets it on the camera's shell, and the composer's caret, which had differed at frame 62 of two recordings, matched in two runs of //web/reel:game_determinism after it","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:12.066253Z","id":"f0de70231b59968a43085b32570ad165fa73ee0b91cdda5b122317cb8afd7142","body":{"detail":"Chromium reports the load of the shell's stream SharedWorker (web/shell/src/stream.ts) to the page but never its end, which hung quiet() for QUIET_MS when the shell reloads mid-film (more.ts, after Approve). The pattern /_clax/shell/stream-worker-*.js ties the camera to the shell's bundle name: a renamed or second SharedWorker would hang a recording again. The framenavigated handler (camera.ts:204) also forgets every in-flight request whose frame cannot be read (a worker's) on any frame's navigation, which may let a frame be taken before such a request lands. A sturdier test would read sec-fetch-dest from the request's headers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"f01239959df1070aacd7a6ded5de476cd55a71aab31aebd9b9fdbda7fd04e476"},"summary":"The deterministic camera skips the shell's SharedWorker script by its URL, and drops a navigated document's requests in flight (worker requests included) on any framenavigated","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/reel.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T03:27:50.727973Z","id":"eb5cae800af6a51623efb1c7554a54ed1900099297732f56a46d90d7199ecafd","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md D8 (amended 2026-10-28): a hosted Clax serves the bundled quickstart at /start/ and sends signed-out visitors there from / (clax_http::hosted::LANDING); no clax.dev artifact is the landing page. [upload] landing_artifact and landing, reel-upload and the README block still assume one, and the bundled page shows the reel only when reel.mp4 and reel-poster.jpg sit beside it (web/quickstart/README.md), which the release does not carry. Options: ship the reel in web/dist/quickstart (a binary that grows by the video's size), serve it from an asset the landing page names by URL, or keep publishing a clax.dev artifact for the reel alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"0f8643036b9d605728c6b64efd4b0a937f89f6f04a1fd5ff28f970f26ba0758f"},"summary":"The reel's upload names a clax.dev landing artifact, but the landing page is now the quickstart the release carries","tags":["reel","landing","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/reel.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:13:46.716315Z","id":"0236f61a70d1be86f66fe8201ea19a7110e152ef3a9db7cec778575f3b4e0719","body":{"detail":"web/reel/config.ts parseReel still requires [upload] with landing_artifact and landing (both empty), and the spec's just reel-upload (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md section 10) was never built. The reel's destinations are now Deploy prod's Stream upload (scripts/reel-stream.mjs) and clax-dev-local; the README GIF (D12) has no destination. Removing [upload] means changing parseReel and its tests (web/reel/config.test.ts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"0f8643036b9d605728c6b64efd4b0a937f89f6f04a1fd5ff28f970f26ba0758f"},"summary":"reel.toml's [upload] table is no longer used: the landing page is not an artifact and the reel goes to Cloudflare Stream","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/reel.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:47:14.234731Z","id":"038c5aa9dda69980d472a8afbd70f4c4bf359d09bdafa4a1eb8d8631ac218733","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ffbdd078e","summary":"Decided by the owner on 2026-10-29: the reel is built from the source at release time, not uploaded beside an artifact. //web/reel:reel builds it (763a6eae6); clax.dev serves it from Cloudflare Stream, uploaded by Deploy prod (scripts/reel-stream.mjs, ffbdd078e), and just clax-dev-local serves it itself (31970d7ec); the landing page's /start/reel.mp4 and reel-poster.jpg redirect there (Hosted::with_reel, 61bc2fc2c). Evidence: hosted_pages::the_landing_pages_reel_redirects_to_where_hosted_mode_serves_it passes in //crates/clax-server:integration__*, and bazelisk build //web/reel:reel wrote a 5,613,221-byte reel.mp4.","supersedes":"eb5cae800af6a51623efb1c7554a54ed1900099297732f56a46d90d7199ecafd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:36.895007Z","id":"5836457cb17db9e3911276784e898c2e3f0fd0604f52bd4b0c845f7a0672fd4e","body":{"detail":"FREEZE_IN keeps each animation's first-seen time in Animation.id, the one piece of per-animation state that every JavaScript world shares (the recorder evaluates in an isolated world or over the DevTools protocol, and getAnimations() hands each world its own wrappers). A page that names its animations, reads their ids, or reads their playState or currentTime would see the recorder's values: a vignette filming such a page would show it behaving differently than it does for a person.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"c0a90d004af08911ad777c0476184cd1adfbe9e17a13b9aa5ae48578a39ad316"},"suggested_fix":"Keep first-seen times recorder-side, keyed by the DevTools protocol's object identity (a RemoteObject per animation in one isolated world held for the frame's life), and leave id alone.","summary":"The deterministic camera writes `reel@<ms>` into the id of every animation on the page, and pauses them through the page's own Animation objects","supersedes":"75f782cc7dede74b4ad3a7359e109f299eb023cdfa39f1f6c9b40dbdd95a8baf","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:36.996925Z","id":"cf441c0dc04e080f0a424604164da89f3b4169c34263fc6e239e64c72ac1630c","body":{"detail":"The caret blinks on the browser's own timer, which page.clock does not hold: //web/reel:agent_determinism failed on frames 173-184 where one run showed the composer's caret and the other did not. Playwright's own screenshots hide the caret by default for the same reason.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":79},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"d0248b0e8ff67da306d76159bcfda68d3e541bed581d558183ddafadf37b341e"},"summary":"The deterministic camera hides every text caret (NO_CARET), so the film shows no caret while Alex types","supersedes":"9d6e385e43cefe45bf1dda81a51a2ccb019811fdf23eb31fb1e5a6d89c0b9ecb","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:37.098971Z","id":"75219bcfb002dde78255995dbff6f55d6bee805497ac61c27b0718d3eba915ad","body":{"detail":"Chromium reports the load of the shell's stream SharedWorker (web/shell/src/stream.ts) to the page but never its end, which hung quiet() for QUIET_MS when the shell reloads mid-film (more.ts, after Approve). The pattern /_clax/shell/stream-worker-*.js ties the camera to the shell's bundle name: a renamed or second SharedWorker would hang a recording again. The framenavigated handler (camera.ts:204) also forgets every in-flight request whose frame cannot be read (a worker's) on any frame's navigation, which may let a frame be taken before such a request lands. A sturdier test would read sec-fetch-dest from the request's headers.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"f01239959df1070aacd7a6ded5de476cd55a71aab31aebd9b9fdbda7fd04e476"},"summary":"The deterministic camera skips the shell's SharedWorker script by its URL, and drops a navigated document's requests in flight (worker requests included) on any framenavigated","supersedes":"f0de70231b59968a43085b32570ad165fa73ee0b91cdda5b122317cb8afd7142","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:37.202196Z","id":"4a04d873dd8da506b1acc35ebf15c592a93025d406187fae544a87ddd65c29ba","body":{"detail":"Measured with web/reel/seed/starchase.html in //web/reel:game_frames: the content frame's first animation frame ran at REEL time +5 ms in one run and +8 ms in another (playwright-core's injected clock, getTimeToNextFrame() = 16 - ticks % 16, ticks counted from the document's own load). Within a 33 ms film frame two or three callbacks run, at times whose phase differs per run, so a page that reads Date.now() or performance.now() per animation frame, or steps once per callback, films different pixels each run, although this comment says animation frames run on the camera's clock. web/reel/seed/starchase.html steps its game on 30ths of a second of Date.now() (ceil((now - 0.5) / (100/3))) to be filmed the same. Pages the reel films with continuous animation need the same, or the camera needs to align each document's animation frames to its film frames.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":181},"end":{"line":183},"content_hash":"64a4f5543c48ddf60a5491543913bc38ea8d8c04ab5bdd7e0a6c9b72c5a80f05"},"summary":"Date.now() read in an animation frame is not the same from run to run under the deterministic camera: Playwright's fake requestAnimationFrame fires on a 16 ms grid of each document's own performance.now() origin","supersedes":"d966bd6e8abce274276c0def826f1e2eece6c136a1aec92d6dde4fd15cef655b","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:37.598232Z","id":"40c0bcdda961a8804a1d49c3e123df503dd2746e47398328e1b4b374e3300724","body":{"detail":"SEEDED_RANDOM (an init script on the camera's context in deterministic mode) replaces Math.random with mulberry32 from one seed, so the shell's backoff jitter (web/shell/src/lifecycle.ts:82, used from page code) and the gallery's random haiku (web/shell/src/view/haiku.ts:5) draw the same numbers each run, as long as the calls come in the same order. The shell's stream runs in a SharedWorker (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts:601 retries with backoff()), where no init script reaches: a stream retry there waits a random, real-time amount. crypto.getRandomValues and crypto.randomUUID are untouched; an ID drawn with them that reaches the screen differs per run.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"e643f97fb275d8641d2f5e7119aa08c36c7a28138902d86f263c931afba5a203"},"suggested_fix":"If a vignette films a stream retry, or shows a client-minted ID, seed the worker through a CDP Target.setAutoAttach session (Runtime.evaluate in the worker before it runs) or keep that state off camera.","summary":"A deterministic camera seeds Math.random in its pages' documents, but not in their workers, and crypto.getRandomValues stays random","supersedes":"f36fff73fc1a61d6083d0a47ed45de82efcc538fc77a157db4690720182fc06c","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:37.706882Z","id":"5fa60b3dd4338aa0104a8c33c478e1dda28eaff604814054a565710154c0d521","body":{"detail":"hostedDaemon in web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts calls test.skip when the daemon takes another port, which only works inside a Playwright test, so the recorder restates its [hosted] config (public_origin, setup_secret_env) and fails instead. Factoring a startHosted() that both call would keep one copy of that config, at the cost of touching the e2e helpers (and so rerunning every browser test) in the reel's first change.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"cf00ca93ad8ce8dff77717c6360b13e077db56b9664e3b5af9a71e2ca9c12f3f"},"summary":"Factor a test-free hosted daemon start out of web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts instead of restating its config here","supersedes":"ec233ccf007effaf05f4008bc36e0a3d9f13da96c9317ad0e5b9e0eb51c776de","tags":["revisit:the [hosted] config hostedDaemon writes changes, or a second recorder needs it","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:37.816334Z","id":"10d1cbbf62333f082fd409f40bb9031f3aed2d53b11988476d5bf83027b77453","body":{"detail":"Playwright's recordVideo scales a page's screencast down to fit the size it is given, never up: at size 1600 × 1000 a 1280 × 800 viewport at device scale 1.25 recorded as 1280 × 800 in the top left corner of a grey 1600 × 1000 frame. So fast mode records at the viewport's size; the capture's 1600 × 1000 device pixels (spec §5) come from deterministic mode (CDP screenshots with a clip at the page's devicePixelRatio, web/reel/camera.ts). A reel composed from fast clips (`reel_fast`, spec §8) must scale them up or frame them smaller.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":159},"content_hash":"a3cd579606f12e65f71cbf8dbb1978c9a7f0b22f2c4122db87f804fe3355af94"},"summary":"The fast clip is 1280 × 800 (the viewport's CSS size), not the capture's 1600 × 1000","supersedes":"d461bfc8551d0a4cdaac125d5912257657f4f9fd0cf0bf59eba39bcd875bc4b1","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:37.917643Z","id":"994d6ae75f6d33acf0089d64d2f2d8963a889bbf7ecfb76b8cedcd34f547246c","body":{"detail":"The camera's context clock starts at REEL_EPOCH (2026-11-03T09:41:00Z) and the deterministic camera rolls at a multiple of 2 s after it; the daemon stamps comments, versions and drafts with the machine's real time. A view that shows a stamp relative to now (\"2 minutes ago\", \"in 7 days\") compares a real time with a fixed one, so it reads oddly and changes from run to run as the real date moves. realtime shows none on camera.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"a61fe77e63d657148116065c55f4ffd58fbf75d15a59fc6af2f63e43323f21d8"},"suggested_fix":"Run the vignette's daemon on a clock fixed to REEL_EPOCH as well (a test-only clock override on the daemon), or keep stamped times off camera.","summary":"Times the daemon stamps are real, while the camera's pages read REEL_EPOCH plus their setup: a relative time between the two is neither fixed nor sensible","supersedes":"310f269349d1583d314a322f924a437d48a61a8f33b3b4f2121456d59dc3b11c","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:56.683133Z","id":"3994ebae9633aa0af7dd97eced803c58cbcf0f792d3853112d09f143bd1b58b8","body":{"detail":"Clicking from the gallery into an artifact (web/reel/vignettes/coldopen.ts, before its keeper tab) made the new page request /_clax/shell/stream-worker-<hash>.js; the page's `request` event added it to `pending`, but no `requestfinished` or `requestfailed` came for it, so quiet() failed: \"a frame waited 10 s on http://localhost:<port>/_clax/shell/stream-worker-J1zpXLYI.js\". The gallery's own load during setup did not hit this, as `pending` is only tracked once the camera rolls. coldopen.ts:131:136 works around it with a second, unfilmed tab on the gallery that keeps the shared worker alive, so the artifact page joins it without fetching its script.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":217},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"23884d5feca40a86fb3f3873f8c5cfb4d67e93368cd08f00d57e6e58276d35f7"},"suggested_fix":"Leave out of `pending` a request made for a worker (its script fetch), or count it done once its response is received; then drop the keeper tab in coldopen.ts.","summary":"A navigation during play fails the deterministic camera: the shell's shared stream worker script is requested and never seen to finish","supersedes":"bf88d144c2882a15dba6728f6024079144bc5225963d67369378d9931114ffbb","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:56.785683Z","id":"fdab4cdfbf732712a07cb30b1250025caf0ccb95deaf6a9eb54bdf49df995317","body":{"detail":"Needed for a Reload during a roll: the old content frame vanished between page.frames() and its lookup, which failed the recording (no frame <v1 url>). The skipped document is reached at the next frame. A document mid-navigation that shows on a screenshot unfrozen could differ between runs; the agent vignette avoids it by waiting for the new shell in the Reload click's `landed` (web/reel/director.ts click), so no frame is taken mid-load. //web/reel:agent_determinism passes.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":293},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"036dee4cbbb0c7f089ff2acc7f787525bcadbd9bd70e0e2e16be5cfd34f56439"},"summary":"inEach skips a frame the page is replacing (detached, or not found in the frame tree by its URL): that document's animations are not frozen and its queue not drained for that one frame","supersedes":"2dcbc3afe05dc5fbec296f60ba2b454e2c102fb3846dfa17b180ce25af06e35f","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:56.885734Z","id":"458578c17c300f9d265983e96fd53f48c5ad7e2a1e0ea407f237d4160716b6a5","body":{"detail":"quiet() waits for the page's in-flight requests (Playwright request events: the page's frames, not its shared or service workers) and then drains each frame's task queue with a MessageChannel round trip, frames inside first and the page last, twice over. A message one renderer posts to another (the artifact frame's clax:peer-at to the shell, which places the name tags) is very likely, not certain, to have run before the screenshot. realtime.ts waits for each person's step to reach Alex's frame (clax:peers, db/changed) before the film moves on; what one renderer then tells another inside a frame is what the drain covers. //web/reel:realtime_determinism passed on its runs on one machine; a failure there names the first differing frame and keeps the pair in the test's outputs.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":321},"end":{"line":338},"content_hash":"b30826569e7a6194a78da269e4a780f42b47fa0c5be4dc576ec0a77661f6ec51"},"suggested_fix":"If a pair ever differs on a tag or arrow, keep the artifact frame in the shell's process for the deterministic camera (Chromium --disable-features=IsolateOrigins,site-per-process, merged with Playwright's own --disable-features list, which a second flag would replace).","summary":"A frame is taken once the page's requests are done and each frame's queued tasks have run, which orders work inside a process but only very likely across processes","supersedes":"1e679dbcaa945d521fb45e7df8a297cf98f4d004366b1a728b8568b05d79ef9c","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:56.988093Z","id":"b863ca86479eaed981a8fdec8477490ef22d48cdeb5fa33580340f69f9100442","body":{"detail":"The deterministic camera steps Playwright's clock and the page's animations, but the text caret's blink is driven by the renderer (its caret blink timer), which neither reaches. realtime films Alex's page with no focused field, so it is not affected; a vignette whose camera types into a field (a composer, a search box) would see frames differ by the caret alone.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":346},"end":{"line":362},"content_hash":"609fb728805f7f719385c2cbc4560e40981dda4e7dd01950f8e76831702f5491"},"suggested_fix":"For a deterministic camera, give focused fields `caret-color: transparent` with an init stylesheet, or draw the caret as the reel's own steady bar; or set the blink interval to 0 if the pinned Chromium honours a flag for it.","summary":"A focused text field's caret blinks on Chromium's own timer, not the page's clock: a vignette that films one gets the caret on or off by real timing","supersedes":"0ff266c9f91ee4046eb8cc4a6cabf9268b02ce575264aea717749ab5d0028479","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:36:03.738900Z","id":"e0432502551d4ca1fbb9ed9f4bb7b8e679f54e5d0a9f2819cfe8efb48486c882","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"comment","references":"b863ca86479eaed981a8fdec8477490ef22d48cdeb5fa33580340f69f9100442","span":{"start":{"line":346},"end":{"line":362},"content_hash":"609fb728805f7f719385c2cbc4560e40981dda4e7dd01950f8e76831702f5491"},"summary":"`caret-animation: manual` on text fields keeps the caret drawn without blinking: web/reel/vignettes/game.ts:66:83 sets it on the camera's shell, and the composer's caret, which had differed at frame 62 of two recordings, matched in two runs of //web/reel:game_determinism after it","supersedes":"9043459ca48abd398e8ca293b6edf8528f0942c4460c54c71df3d488b03c3c11","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
